00:56:50,642 --> 00:56:52,310
[ Panting ]

1478
00:56:53,645 --> 00:56:56,948
SERVO: Great. I'm gonna buy
some liver snaps and a hasta.

1479
00:56:58,950 --> 00:57:02,020
CROW: I've always wanted
a tan Yugo.

1480
00:57:02,053 --> 00:57:03,755
MAN: Hey, what the hell?
That's my car.

1481
00:57:03,788 --> 00:57:05,123
SERVO: Wait.
The clutch kind of sticks,

1482
00:57:05,157 --> 00:57:07,458
and one door doesn't close,
and you got to jiggle it

1483
00:57:07,492 --> 00:57:09,427
to get into reverse!

1484
00:57:09,460 --> 00:57:10,595
[ Car engine revving ]

1485
00:57:10,628 --> 00:57:12,063
-SERVO: Huh?
-EDDIE: Whoa.

1486
00:57:12,097 --> 00:57:13,965
Yeah, I did that
on my first driver's test.

1487
00:57:13,998 --> 00:57:16,067
I was still kind of drunk
from the night before.

1488
00:57:16,100 --> 00:57:17,568
SERVO: [ Laughs ]

1489
00:57:17,602 --> 00:57:20,138
CROW: We also raise llamas,
if you like to pet a llama.

1490
00:57:20,172 --> 00:57:21,372
[ Grunts ]

1491
00:57:21,405 --> 00:57:23,575
My car! My car!

1492
00:57:23,608 --> 00:57:25,743
What the hell
did you do to my car?

1493
00:57:25,777 --> 00:57:28,445
EDDIE: It drives
like a Kennedy, you idiot.

1494
00:57:28,480 --> 00:57:30,113
I don't drive.

1495
00:57:31,282 --> 00:57:33,785
SERVO: I got a dead alien
in the attic.

1496
00:57:33,818 --> 00:57:34,985
Okay.

1497
00:57:35,018 --> 00:57:36,487
CROW: Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa,
whoa, whoa!

1498
00:57:36,520 --> 00:57:39,090
[ Car engine revving ]

1499
00:57:40,158 --> 00:57:41,558
SERVO: Hmm?

1500
00:57:41,592 --> 00:57:43,795
Ah-ha!
So, it's bicycles, then, eh?

1501
00:57:43,828 --> 00:57:46,397
We accept your choice
of vehicle. En garde!

1502
00:57:46,430 --> 00:57:47,465
[ Music playing ]

1503
00:57:47,498 --> 00:57:49,033
CROW: This is
a very healthy chase.

1504
00:57:50,602 --> 00:57:53,137
EDDIE: Well, I'll just give you
a warning this time.

1505
00:57:54,605 --> 00:57:56,975
CROW: Oh, a K-car,
come right through, ma'am.

1506
00:58:02,613 --> 00:58:04,915
SERVO: She's doing caricatures
of the victims.

1507
00:58:04,948 --> 00:58:05,950
CROW: Wow.

1508
00:58:05,983 --> 00:58:07,852
-Any survivors?
-Are you kidding?

1509
00:58:07,885 --> 00:58:10,622
We'll be lucky
if we get dental records.

1510
00:58:10,655 --> 00:58:12,290
How many were on board?

1511
00:58:12,323 --> 00:58:13,525
It looks like just one.

1512
00:58:13,558 --> 00:58:14,758
Any idea how old?

1513
00:58:14,792 --> 00:58:18,262
Can you tell how stale bread is
after it's been toasted?

1514
00:58:18,295 --> 00:58:19,263
CROW: Whoa.

1515
00:58:19,297 --> 00:58:20,665
Any make on the plane?

1516
00:58:20,698 --> 00:58:22,500
Yeah. Hey, wait a minute.
Who are you?

1517
00:58:22,533 --> 00:58:24,635
I'm with The Banner.
My name is Lisa Henson.

1518
00:58:24,668 --> 00:58:26,337
CROW:
And I'm a hard boiled reporter.

1519
00:58:26,370 --> 00:58:27,772
Well, from the numbers we got,

1520
00:58:27,805 --> 00:58:31,708
it looks like it belongs
to a Nick Miller.

1521
00:58:31,742 --> 00:58:33,545
It came up from that airport
across the lake.

1522
00:58:33,578 --> 00:58:34,712
EDDIE:
She's a really good actress.

1523
00:58:34,745 --> 00:58:35,713
SERVO: Yeah.
You're right, Eddie.

1524
00:58:35,747 --> 00:58:37,382
EDDIE: Hey, shut up.
She is not.

1525
00:58:37,415 --> 00:58:39,517
EDDIE: I'm kidding.

1526
00:58:40,252 --> 00:58:41,552
SERVO: I'm sorry.

1527
00:58:42,520 --> 00:58:43,722
CROW: The cameraman's shy.

1528
00:58:43,755 --> 00:58:46,157
Come on, honey.
You can get closer.

1529
00:58:46,190 --> 00:58:47,525
Come on.

1530
00:58:47,558 --> 00:58:48,627
-That's...
-MATT: ...a millionaire.

1531
00:58:48,660 --> 00:58:51,162
Nick, really, this is the most
incredible thing.

1532
00:58:51,195 --> 00:58:52,463
Great.

1533
00:58:52,497 --> 00:58:53,865
-So, what's the next step?
-Well, like I said,

1534
00:58:53,898 --> 00:58:55,800
I'm going to go over
the heads of my bosses

1535
00:58:55,833 --> 00:58:57,402
and take this directly
to J.K. Robertson.

1536
00:58:57,435 --> 00:58:58,570
When?

1537
00:58:58,603 --> 00:59:01,005
Well, I'll be back
with Mr. Robertson at...

1538
00:59:01,038 --> 00:59:02,173
SERVO: Dark 30.

1539
00:59:02,207 --> 00:59:03,507
4:00 p.m., is that okay?

1540
00:59:03,540 --> 00:59:04,708
Fine. I'll be ready.

1541
00:59:04,742 --> 00:59:06,243
Great. Great.
Oh, and, Nick,

1542
00:59:06,277 --> 00:59:08,713
in the meantime,
don't tell anyone about this,

1543
00:59:08,747 --> 00:59:10,382
and I mean, anyone.

1544
00:59:10,415 --> 00:59:12,317
Trust me on this, okay?

1545
00:59:12,350 --> 00:59:13,550
-All right.
-Great.

1546
00:59:13,585 --> 00:59:16,687
We are going to be very rich!

1547
00:59:16,720 --> 00:59:18,355
[ Music playing ]

1548
00:59:18,388 --> 00:59:21,692
CROW: [ Humming ]

1549
00:59:21,725 --> 00:59:24,095
SERVO: When really short guys
try to walk.

1550
00:59:26,630 --> 00:59:30,067
EDDIE: Oh, yeah, the throaty
roar of a K-car.

1551
00:59:31,802 --> 00:59:34,338
CROW: They somehow gave her
plaid theme music.

1552
00:59:34,372 --> 00:59:37,642
SERVO: Mr. Blackwell put her
on his "Please Kill" list.

1553
00:59:41,812 --> 00:59:43,447
EDDIE: All right.
We're finally gonna see

1554
00:59:43,480 --> 00:59:46,350
some horizontal rumba or what?

1555
00:59:46,383 --> 00:59:47,418
CROW: Eddie.

1556
00:59:47,452 --> 00:59:49,053
-Lisa?
-Nick.

1557
00:59:49,087 --> 00:59:50,788
CROW: I shaved this morning
and got a nick.

1558
00:59:50,822 --> 00:59:52,123
-How are you?
-CROW: Ow.

1559
00:59:52,157 --> 00:59:53,223
Good. I'm good.

1560
00:59:53,257 --> 00:59:53,825
EDDIE: You're all right.

1561
00:59:53,858 --> 00:59:55,125
-Get up here.
-Yeah.

1562
00:59:55,158 --> 00:59:57,895
-CROW: Golly, Edward.
-...must not have heard yet.

1563
00:59:57,928 --> 00:59:59,597
-SERVO: Okay.
-EDDIE: He's fine.

1564
00:59:59,630 --> 01:00:01,898
I work for The Banner
in town now.

1565
01:00:01,932 --> 01:00:04,935
I was called to--
your grandmother...

1566
01:00:04,968 --> 01:00:07,905
Her plane crashed
over by the lake.

1567
01:00:07,938 --> 01:00:10,908
What?
What are you talking about?

1568
01:00:10,942 --> 01:00:13,043
LISA: It exploded on impact.

1569
01:00:13,077 --> 01:00:14,912
I'm sorry. I thought you
would have heard by now.

1570
01:00:14,945 --> 01:00:19,217
NICK: Lisa, my grandparents died
when you and I were kids.

1571
01:00:19,250 --> 01:00:21,752
That's right.
But you called the paper.

1572
01:00:21,785 --> 01:00:23,553
I was just trying to get
someone to come out

1573
01:00:23,587 --> 01:00:24,888
and take a look at this.

1574
01:00:24,922 --> 01:00:26,090
LISA: The plane
was registered to you.

1575
01:00:26,123 --> 01:00:27,825
-It was one of your planes.
-But, Lisa, I only owned...

1576
01:00:27,858 --> 01:00:29,927
-TOM: One jar of mustard.
-...one plane.

1577
01:00:29,960 --> 01:00:30,795
LISA: Registration number

1578
01:00:30,828 --> 01:00:35,333
is N5--
058C.

1579
01:00:35,367 --> 01:00:36,533
That's right.

1580
01:00:39,103 --> 01:00:42,040
[ Music playing ]

1581
01:00:43,473 --> 01:00:45,643
CROW: We listen now
to the Jefferson Middle School

1582
01:00:45,677 --> 01:00:47,312
String Quartet.

1583
01:00:48,780 --> 01:00:50,815
EDDIE: Yup. Grandma came
back from the dead,

1584
01:00:50,848 --> 01:00:52,850
built a duplicate plane,
and crashed it.

1585
01:00:52,883 --> 01:00:55,318
-It's my plane.
-Then what's going on?

1586
01:00:55,353 --> 01:00:57,622
SERVO: It's time chasers.

1587
01:00:57,655 --> 01:00:59,123
We need to take a little trip.

1588
01:01:00,392 --> 01:01:04,695
CROW: We need to go out for some
Amish fudge, it'd be nice.

1589
01:01:04,728 --> 01:01:08,665
SERVO:
♪ Walking on broken glass ♪

1590
01:01:08,700 --> 01:01:10,835
♪ Walking on, walking on ♪

1591
01:01:11,835 --> 01:01:13,905
EDDIE: What,
is he at the pound?

1592
01:01:17,575 --> 01:01:19,743
CROW: [ Buzzing noise ]

1593
01:01:21,512 --> 01:01:25,883
EDDIE: ♪ Cisco Kid
was a friend of mine ♪

1594
01:01:25,917 --> 01:01:26,817
SERVO: It's really good, Eddie.

1595
01:01:26,850 --> 01:01:28,753
CROW: You would like that,
wouldn't you?

1596
01:01:30,388 --> 01:01:32,057
Remember when everyone
got the Nick Miller haircut

1597
01:01:32,090 --> 01:01:34,725
and started wearing
Castleton T-shirts?

1598
01:01:34,758 --> 01:01:37,062
SERVO: Missed the barn dance.

1599
01:01:37,095 --> 01:01:40,163
Oh, where the hell is my plane?
[ Servo makes farting noise ]

1600
01:01:40,197 --> 01:01:41,898
MAN: Well, Nick...

1601
01:01:42,900 --> 01:01:44,702
It seems you forgot
you were in the past.

1602
01:01:44,735 --> 01:01:45,837
SERVO: You varmint.

1603
01:01:45,870 --> 01:01:49,107
[ Music playing ]

1604
01:01:52,077 --> 01:01:54,978
CROW: Say you like Northwest,
go ahead.

1605
01:01:55,012 --> 01:01:57,248
You're a drug dealer.
You're a drug dealer.

1606
01:01:57,282 --> 01:01:59,250
EDDIE: [ mimics speaker ]
SERVO: It's funny.

1607
01:01:59,283 --> 01:02:00,918
There's no way you
can afford all this stuff

1608
01:02:00,952 --> 01:02:02,420
on a teacher's salary.
Electronics, radar...

1609
01:02:02,453 --> 01:02:04,922
Look, Marty, I don't know
how to tell you this, you know,

1610
01:02:04,955 --> 01:02:06,157
but we got a serious
problem right here.

1611
01:02:06,190 --> 01:02:07,525
Tell me anything.

1612
01:02:07,558 --> 01:02:09,727
J.K.: Look, gentlemen,
Say goodbye to this century.

1613
01:02:09,760 --> 01:02:11,862
Look, leave Marty here.

1614
01:02:11,895 --> 01:02:12,897
He doesn't know what's going on.

1615
01:02:12,930 --> 01:02:13,898
J.K.: Sorry.

1616
01:02:13,932 --> 01:02:16,833
He knows enough
to disrupt your past self.

1617
01:02:16,867 --> 01:02:18,035
They're gonna kill us.

1618
01:02:18,903 --> 01:02:20,938
I'm gonna make you
a part of history.

1619
01:02:20,972 --> 01:02:24,342
CROW: Oh, is that a sexual
overture of some kind?

1620
01:02:24,375 --> 01:02:25,443
EDDIE: Look at that.

1621
01:02:25,477 --> 01:02:26,743
There's too many sevens
in that date.

1622
01:02:26,777 --> 01:02:29,080
I'm going out for a smoke.

1623
01:02:29,113 --> 01:02:29,913
SERVO: Okay.

1624
01:02:29,947 --> 01:02:31,748
Do that, Eddie. Enjoy.

1625
01:02:31,782 --> 01:02:32,883
CROW: Can he do that?

1626
01:02:34,118 --> 01:02:39,257
SERVO: ♪ All my friends
driving lowriders. ♪

1627
01:02:39,290 --> 01:02:40,390
NICK: Marty?

1628
01:02:40,423 --> 01:02:42,993
CROW: Hey, Marty,
let's do lunch, Marty.

1629
01:02:44,995 --> 01:02:47,398
SERVO: Wow,
the present is amazing.

1630
01:02:48,765 --> 01:02:51,868
That was absolutely incredible.

1631
01:02:51,902 --> 01:02:54,738
CROW: It's me,
your cousin, Saul.

1632
01:02:54,772 --> 01:02:57,875
-Where is the phone?
-Marty?

1633
01:02:57,908 --> 01:03:00,945
CROW: Let's get some
blintzes, Marty.

1634
01:03:00,978 --> 01:03:02,847
NICK: I'll meet you,
and then we'll go up. Marty?

1635
01:03:02,880 --> 01:03:05,115
SERVO: Oh, bacon grease.

1636
01:03:05,148 --> 01:03:06,117
NICK: Who are you calling?

1637
01:03:06,150 --> 01:03:07,652
SERVO: Are you okay there,
Eddie?

1638
01:03:07,685 --> 01:03:09,453
Slow as they are, they should
have a dental record

1639
01:03:09,487 --> 01:03:11,288
matched for an ID by now.

1640
01:03:11,322 --> 01:03:13,790
NICK: I have got a demo
with Gen-Corp in two hours.

1641
01:03:13,825 --> 01:03:16,127
And he's probably out getting
drunk somewhere.

1642
01:03:16,160 --> 01:03:19,430
LISA: Yes. This is
Lisa Henson of The Banner.

1643
01:03:19,463 --> 01:03:21,065
We're doing a story
on the plane crash.

1644
01:03:21,098 --> 01:03:24,968
I was wondering if you
had an ID on the pilot yet?

1645
01:03:25,002 --> 01:03:25,937
Yes, with The Banner.

1646
01:03:25,970 --> 01:03:27,438
SERVO: It was the Shopper-News.

1647
01:03:27,472 --> 01:03:28,538
Yeah, that's me.

1648
01:03:29,307 --> 01:03:31,075
No, this isn't a joke.

1649
01:03:31,108 --> 01:03:33,878
CROW: Myrtle Johnson
didn't serve lemon bars?

1650
01:03:35,513 --> 01:03:36,647
Are you sure?

1651
01:03:36,680 --> 01:03:39,417
SERVO: I should have
checked my sources.

1652
01:03:39,450 --> 01:03:42,520
Must be. Thank you.

1653
01:03:43,787 --> 01:03:45,188
EDDIE: Hey, watch,
the door is gonna hit her

1654
01:03:45,222 --> 01:03:46,823
in the can when he comes in.

1655
01:03:46,857 --> 01:03:49,060
CROW: That would be great,
Eddie.

1656
01:03:51,728 --> 01:03:52,930
Well?

1657
01:03:52,963 --> 01:03:54,832
The person they identified
as being killed

1658
01:03:54,865 --> 01:03:55,867
in the plane crash...

1659
01:03:55,900 --> 01:03:57,802
SERVO: Was Daryl Dragon.

1660
01:03:57,835 --> 01:03:59,870
...was Lisa Henson
of The Banner.

1661
01:03:59,903 --> 01:04:02,038
CROW:
Oh, well, that's a big loss.

1662
01:04:04,042 --> 01:04:07,077
-I'm dead?
-SERVO: Well, then, fall down!

1663
01:04:10,982 --> 01:04:13,583
Hey, the New England Patriots!

1664
01:04:17,020 --> 01:04:18,388
CROW: Someday a lot
of puffy old losers

1665
01:04:18,422 --> 01:04:20,825
with no life will reenact
this battle, men.

1666
01:04:20,858 --> 01:04:22,560
MAN: Muskets steady.

1667
01:04:22,593 --> 01:04:25,195
SERVO: You're going
into battle in that outfit?

1668
01:04:27,832 --> 01:04:30,267
CROW:
Ted Nugent's family reunion.

1669
01:04:34,605 --> 01:04:37,608
SERVO: Just try to go, Harry.
We're not watching.

1670
01:04:41,778 --> 01:04:44,048
CROW: Dr. Demento, patriot.

1671
01:04:45,382 --> 01:04:48,252
SERVO: Oh, good thing
the minutemen built a runway.

1672
01:04:52,690 --> 01:04:55,927
CROW: General Washington's
plane has landed.

1673
01:04:57,127 --> 01:05:00,698
SERVO: We are going
to the company picnic, damn it.

1674
01:05:06,103 --> 01:05:08,038
Listen, I understand limits,
Matt,

1675
01:05:08,072 --> 01:05:10,073
but this has to be done to wipe
the slate clean,

1676
01:05:10,107 --> 01:05:12,108
they'll just be unaccounted
war dead here.

1677
01:05:12,142 --> 01:05:13,110
I know, I know.

1678
01:05:13,143 --> 01:05:15,212
But I can't be a part of it.

1679
01:05:15,245 --> 01:05:18,015
I'll wait back at the transport
if you want me to, but...

1680
01:05:18,048 --> 01:05:19,617
-Sorry, J.K.
-That's all right.

1681
01:05:19,650 --> 01:05:21,052
I can handle this myself.

1682
01:05:21,085 --> 01:05:23,087
I'll see you back
at the transport in a minute.

1683
01:05:23,120 --> 01:05:25,088
Okay. Okay.

1684
01:05:25,122 --> 01:05:27,725
CROW: There goes
a damn good weenie.

1685
01:05:29,427 --> 01:05:30,728
Oh, Matt?

1686
01:05:30,762 --> 01:05:32,128
I changed my mind.

1687
01:05:32,162 --> 01:05:33,397
You're fired.
[ Gunshots ]

1688
01:05:33,430 --> 01:05:35,700
SERVO: He's still a better boss
than the Sunbeam guy.

1689
01:05:35,733 --> 01:05:38,035
Now, what were we talking about?

1690
01:05:38,068 --> 01:05:40,103
Oh, yes, history.

1691
01:05:40,137 --> 01:05:43,073
MAN: Put that weapon down.

1692
01:05:43,107 --> 01:05:45,308
SERVO: Huzzah,
I think, I'm not sure.

1693
01:05:45,342 --> 01:05:46,977
Whoa, minutemen.

1694
01:05:47,010 --> 01:05:49,913
Correction,
they are pissed minutemen.

1695
01:05:49,947 --> 01:05:51,115
Lisa?

1696
01:05:51,148 --> 01:05:53,050
I am not believing this.

1697
01:05:53,083 --> 01:05:54,052
I told them the truth,
Robertson.

1698
01:05:54,085 --> 01:05:55,052
The truth?

1699
01:05:55,085 --> 01:05:56,753
They know you're a spy
working for the British,

1700
01:05:56,787 --> 01:05:58,488
and they aren't letting you
out of this forest.

1701
01:05:58,522 --> 01:06:00,457
Don't play games
with your life, Nick.

1702
01:06:00,490 --> 01:06:02,827
This is an Uzi.
You're out-gunned.

1703
01:06:02,860 --> 01:06:04,662
For God's sake, give them fire.

1704
01:06:04,695 --> 01:06:05,730
[ Gunshot ]

1705
01:06:05,763 --> 01:06:07,398
CROW: So, history
is just circling the drain

1706
01:06:07,432 --> 01:06:10,167
-at this point, I guess.
-SERVO: Yup.

1707
01:06:10,200 --> 01:06:13,603
[ Music playing ]

1708
01:06:13,637 --> 01:06:15,740
SERVO: And so, children,
the British defeated us

1709
01:06:15,773 --> 01:06:17,442
because they were all helping
this lunkhead

1710
01:06:17,475 --> 01:06:19,077
who whizzed history
down his leg.

1711
01:06:19,110 --> 01:06:20,010
LISA:
Hey, where are they going?

1712
01:06:20,043 --> 01:06:21,012
Come back!

1713
01:06:21,045 --> 01:06:22,813
I don't think
they've ever seen an Uzi.

1714
01:06:22,847 --> 01:06:24,748
[ Gunshots ]

1715
01:06:24,782 --> 01:06:26,317
No place to run.

